# Frontend Architecture Rules

> These rules are extracted from the existing codebase. Follow them strictly to maintain architectural consistency.

---

## 1. Framework & Runtime

- **Next.js 14 App Router** is the framework. Never use Pages Router patterns (`getServerSideProps`, `getStaticProps`, `_app.tsx`, `_document.tsx`).
- Prefer **Server Components** by default. Only add `"use client"` when the component needs browser APIs, event handlers, hooks, or state.
- Use **Route Groups** `(auth)`, `(dashboard)` to organize layouts without affecting URLs.

---

## 2. Component Declaration & Exports

- Declare components as **named function declarations**, not arrow-function constants:
  ```tsx
  // ✅ Correct
  export function MyComponent({ title }: MyComponentProps) { ... }

  // ❌ Wrong
  const MyComponent: React.FC<MyComponentProps> = ({ title }) => { ... }
  export default MyComponent;
  ```
- Use **named exports**. Avoid `export default` on components.
- One primary component per file. File name must match the exported component name in PascalCase.

---

## 3. Props & Types

- Define props with an **`interface`** named `<ComponentName>Props`, placed directly above the component:
  ```tsx
  interface KPICardProps {
    title: string;
    value: string;
    trend: "up" | "down" | "neutral";
  }

  export function KPICard({ title, value, trend }: KPICardProps) { ... }
  ```
- Use **string literal unions** for enum-like values (statuses, roles, priorities), not TypeScript `enum`:
  ```tsx
  // ✅ Correct
  type TicketStatus = "open" | "in_progress" | "resolved" | "closed";

  // ❌ Wrong
  enum TicketStatus { Open, InProgress, Resolved, Closed }
  ```
- Place shared/domain types in `src/types/`. Keep component-local types in the component file.
- Do not duplicate type definitions across files. Import from the canonical source.

---

## 4. Component Structure Order

Inside every component file, maintain this order:
1. Imports
2. Props interface / local types
3. Local constants and helper functions
4. Component function declaration
5. `useState` / hooks at the top of the function body
6. Derived/computed values
7. Event handlers
8. JSX return

---

## 5. State Management

- **No external state library** (no Zustand, Redux, Recoil, Jotai). Do not introduce one.
- Use **`useState`** for local component state. Group related state logically.
- Use **React Context** only for cross-cutting concerns (e.g., locale/i18n via `LocaleContext`). Do not create a Context for single-component state.
- For form state in wizards or multi-step flows, use multiple `useState` hooks with clear naming (matching the current `AddTenantWizard` pattern).

---

## 6. Styling — Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui

- **Tailwind utility classes** are the only styling mechanism. Do not use CSS modules, styled-components, or inline `style` objects.
- Use the **`cn()` utility** (from `@/components/ui/utils`) for conditional/merged classes:
  ```tsx
  import { cn } from "@/components/ui/utils";

  <div className={cn("rounded-lg p-4", isActive && "bg-primary text-primary-foreground")} />
  ```
- `cn()` wraps `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`. Always use it when combining dynamic classes.
- Use **CSS custom properties** defined in `src/styles/globals.css` for design tokens (colors, radii, etc.). Reference them via Tailwind's `var()` integration, not raw hex values.

---

## 7. UI Primitives — shadcn/ui + Radix

- All base UI components live in `src/components/ui/`. These wrap **Radix UI primitives** with Tailwind styling and **class-variance-authority (CVA)** for variants.
- Never modify Radix behavior. Only style via CVA `variants` and `cn()` overrides.
- When adding a new primitive, follow the existing pattern:
  ```tsx
  import * as DialogPrimitive from "@radix-ui/react-dialog";
  import { cn } from "@/components/ui/utils";

  const DialogContent = React.forwardRef<...>(({ className, ...props }, ref) => (
    <DialogPrimitive.Content ref={ref} className={cn("...", className)} {...props} />
  ));
  ```
- Use **`forwardRef`** on all UI primitives that wrap Radix elements.
- Import UI components from `@/components/ui/<component>`, not directly from Radix or other libraries.

---

## 8. Icons

- Use **`lucide-react`** exclusively for icons. Do not import from other icon libraries.
  ```tsx
  import { Settings, ChevronDown } from "lucide-react";
  ```

---

## 9. Notifications / Toasts

- Use **`sonner`** (via the `@/components/ui/sonner` wrapper) for toast notifications.
- Do not use `window.alert`, `window.confirm`, or other browser dialogs.

---

## 10. API Calls & Server Actions

- **No Axios.** The project uses the native `fetch` API.
- For **server-side data fetching**, use the `serverFetch` wrapper from `@/lib/api.ts`. It automatically:
  - Reads the `jwt_token` cookie
  - Attaches the `Authorization: Bearer` header
  - Redirects to `/login` on 401 responses
- For **mutations** (login, logout, form submissions), use **Next.js Server Actions** (`"use server"` modules in `src/actions/`):
  ```tsx
  // src/actions/auth.ts
  "use server";
  export async function loginAction(prevState: any, formData: FormData) { ... }
  ```
- In client components, consume server actions with `useFormState` and `useFormStatus` from `react-dom`:
  ```tsx
  const [state, formAction] = useFormState(loginAction, initialState);
  ```
- Never call APIs directly from client components. Always go through `serverFetch` (SSR) or Server Actions (mutations).

---

## 11. Forms

- For **auth/simple forms**: use the native `<form action={...}>` pattern with Server Actions + `useFormState`/`useFormStatus`.
- For **complex multi-step forms** (wizards): use controlled `useState` with manual validation (matching `AddTenantWizard` pattern).
- A `react-hook-form` integration layer exists in `@/components/ui/form.tsx`. Use it when building forms that benefit from field-level validation and error display via the `<FormField>`, `<FormItem>`, `<FormLabel>`, `<FormMessage>` composition.
- Do not mix form strategies within a single form.

---

## 12. Charts

- Use **`recharts`** for all data visualization.
- Wrap recharts components in custom chart components under `src/components/charts/`.
- Use barrel exports via `src/components/charts/index.ts`.
- Follow the existing pattern: each chart type gets its own file (`AreaChart.tsx`, `LineChart.tsx`, `DonutChart.tsx`, `ColumnChart.tsx`).
- Shared formatting/tooltip logic lives in `src/components/charts/utils.ts` and `ChartTooltip.tsx`.

---

## 13. Routing & Layouts

- Keep route files thin. Pages should fetch data (if server component) and render a view component from `src/components/`.
- **Dashboard layouts**: fetch the user via `serverFetch` in the layout, pass to the shell component.
- **Auth guard**: handled by `frontend/middleware.ts` which checks `jwt_token` cookie. Do not duplicate auth checks in individual pages unless RBAC-specific.
- RBAC page-level guards follow the pattern in `(dashboard)/overview/page.tsx` — check `user.role` and render `<RBACOverlay>` for unauthorized roles.

---

## 14. Drag & Drop

- Use **`react-dnd`** with the HTML5 backend for drag-and-drop interactions (e.g., ticket workboard).
- Do not introduce alternative DnD libraries.

---

## 15. Theming

- Use **`next-themes`** for dark/light mode toggling. It integrates with the shadcn/ui `sonner` wrapper.
- Theme tokens are CSS variables in `src/styles/globals.css`.

---

## 16. File Organization

```
frontend/src/
├── actions/          # Server Actions (mutations)
├── app/              # Next.js App Router pages & layouts
│   ├── (auth)/       # Auth route group (login, register)
│   └── (dashboard)/  # Dashboard route group
├── components/       # Feature components (views, shells, forms)
│   ├── charts/       # Recharts wrapper components
│   └── ui/           # shadcn/ui primitives (do not put feature code here)
├── contexts/         # React Context providers
├── lib/              # Utilities, API helpers, data, i18n
├── styles/           # Global CSS with design tokens
└── types/            # TypeScript type definitions
```

- **Do not** put business/feature logic in `components/ui/`.
- **Do not** create new top-level directories without discussion.

---

## 17. Import Aliases

- Use the `@/` path alias for all imports from `src/`:
  ```tsx
  import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
  import { serverFetch } from "@/lib/api";
  ```
- Never use relative paths that go more than one level up (`../../`).
